    "definitions": {
      "frontier": "the per-cell and global CSS Pareto frontiers over (n, k, d, w), the same cell_frontiers and pareto that award the star; cells nest, so a code counts in every cell it qualifies for",
      "leader": "the cell member with the largest kd^2/n (ties: earliest date, then slug)",
      "incumbent": "the same leader over the cell's literature baselines alone (provenance.origin baseline); null when the cell has none",
      "moved": "the leader's declared family differs from the incumbent's",
      "untagged": "records rendered as family other, the default for an entry without a family tag; in every denominator, never a family",
      "hhi": "sum of squared shares of the named families over the frontier's records, from 1/families (even split) to 1 (one family)"
    },
    "caveat": "family is the one self-declared label on an entry, filterable and never ranked, so these shares measure the declared tag, not a property recovered from H; the derived provenance buckets are the computed axis wherever they cover an entry"
